        "paragraphs": [
            "inclusionAI Ling is a family of MoE LLM models provided and open-sourced by inclusionAI. The developer says the family includes two different sizes, Ling-lite and Ling-plus. Ling-lite has 16.8 billion parameters with 2.75 billion activated parameters, while Ling-plus has 290 billion parameters with 28.8 billion activated parameters. inclusionAI says both models demonstrate impressive performance compared to existing models in the industry. The developer also says their structure makes it easy to scale up and down and adapt to different tasks, so users can use these models for a wide range of tasks, from processing natural language to solving complex problems.",
            "The family also includes Ling-lite-base-1.5, Ling-lite-1.5, Ling-plus-base, Ling-coder-lite-base and Ling-coder-lite. Ling-lite-1.5 was released on 2025-5-10 and inclusionAI says it achieves significant progress in reasoning ability compared with previous Ling-lite. Ling-lite was upgraded to Ling-lite-0415 on 2025-4-15, and the developer says the new model demonstrates notable improvements over its predecessor, Ling-lite-0220, especially on code and math. Ling-lite-1.5 has a context length of 128K, Ling-plus-base has 64K, and Ling-coder-lite-base has 16K.",
            "inclusionAI offers the models for download on Hugging Face and ModelScope. For users located in mainland China, the developer also provides the model on ModelScope.cn to speed up the download process. The developer says the open-source nature of Ling promotes collaboration and innovation within the AI community, fostering a diverse range of use cases and enhancements."
        ],
