    "family_reading": {
        "text": "inclusionAI Ling is a small family of five versions, all sharing a 262144 token context window and a 32768 token maximum output. All five support reasoning, and two of the five publish open weights, so open weights are available but not the norm across the line. Inputs can include image, text and video, while output is text only. Pricing varies by version, from free to 0.04 per million input tokens and 0.12 per million output tokens. The facts suggest the family suits long document or long video work that also needs reasoning, with the free and low cost versions attractive for high volume use. Limits are the text only output, the modest output ceiling relative to the context window, and the fact that most versions are API only.",
